    history=f'''<section class="page-title"><div class="eyebrow">Historical review · Owner-reported scores</div><h1>One score belongs<br>to one prediction field.</h1><p>24 supplied sibling URLs reviewed via immutable GitHub source; 32 numeric score entries in the brief. Roots linking to deeper docs were followed. Source reads do not certify the deployed HTTP page or a private submission receipt.</p></section><section class="content"><div class="notice"><strong>Historical evidence, not authenticated leaderboard receipts.</strong>Repeated fingerprints, renamed copies, stale “best score” banners and incomparable local protocols are not independent evidence of model improvement. Unscored and unspecified entries remain unknown.</div><div class="evidence-links">{link('../sources/reported_scores.csv','Download all reported scores · CSV','text-link',download=True)}{link('../evidence/sibling_site_review.json','24 immutable source reviews ↗','text-link')}{link('../knowledge/sibling-review.md','Cross-site conclusions & irregularities ↗','text-link')}</div><div class="search-row"><label for="history-search">Find a repository or submission<input type="search" id="history-search" placeholder="e.g. H25, 16GEMSDOE, lattice" autocomplete="off"></label><span id="history-count">{len(historical)} records shown</span></div><div class="table-wrap"><table id="history-table" class="history-table"><thead><tr><th>Project / source</th><th>Filename in owner brief</th><th>Reported DTI</th><th>Evidence status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(historical)}</tbody></table></div><p class="table-note">The complete repeated prompt is preserved in README. Entries named 25/26/27 with no URL, file or score are not treated as reviewed independent submissions. H26 and H27 have blocked local research artifacts only; no live contest score is claimed.</p><h2>What the history supports</h2><div class="grid3"><article class="card"><h3>Dotting can reduce metric cost</h3><p>GEMSDOE10 reports H25 context-ridge 0.1280 → H28 dotted-ridge 0.1839; H19-5 → H25-1 reports 0.1922 → 0.2477. These are different detectors/protocols. Our H25 operator and local credit reduction were reproduced, not merely assumed.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>A catalogue win can fail live</h3><p>17GEMSDOE advertises dense holdout 0.2795 for D and 0.1524 for F, while the owner reports only 0.0187 for F. GEMSDOE4's mixed-OOF union and noisy selection are disclosed upstream. Proxy improvement is not unknown-fault accuracy.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>More certainty needs evidence</h3><p>Legacy claims of unbiased PU calibration, verified physical fault behaviour, hidden density from one score, guaranteed score reproduction and a known range-error cause exceed their available evidence. We do not inherit them as facts.</p></article></div><h2>H25: same bytes, separate reference</h2><p class="small-note">The reference download is the exact historical file, SHA {ESC(reference['sha256'])}. Its filename here is a descriptive archive label, not a new prediction. Do not resubmit merely to give it a new name.</p>{link('../'+reference['path'],'↓ Historical H25-1 TIFF · do not resubmit','button secondary',download=True)}</section>'''
