    review=f'''<section class="page-title"><div class="eyebrow">Review · Limits · Next session</div><h1>Own the result.<br>Protect the next test.</h1><p>The engineering pipeline is real; the scientific performance gate failed. An exact-format download is not a winning submission. This page keeps the request, verification and remaining blockers aligned.</p></section><section class="content"><h2>Recorded implementation/review passes</h2><p class="small-note">The latest entries record the H27 result reconciliation, code/provenance review and public-site verification. Every pass records engineering checks separately from the failed scientific gate.</p><ul class="audit-list pass-list">{review_list}</ul><div class="evidence-links">{link('../evidence/reviews.json','Recorded review log ↗')}{link('../evidence/reproduction.json','Exact cold pipeline replay ↗')}{link('../evidence/browser_export_checks.json','Actual browser TIFF identity ↗')}{link('../knowledge/requirement-matrix.md','Original request acceptance matrix ↗')}{link('../evidence/site_checks.json','Local files / links / hashes ↗')}{link('../evidence/browser_checks.json','Browser / downloads / UI checks ↗')}</div><h2>Not completed, and not claimed</h2><ul><li><strong>A competition-ready candidate or score above 0.2477 / 0.3195:</strong> H27 failed and produced no TIFF; the downloadable XEDGE file is a blocked OOF research artifact. No external score or upload occurred.</li><li><strong>Independent unknown-fault validation:</strong> catalogue-thinning sensitivity is not hidden truth, and many sibling experiments reuse this area. Historical H25 all-catalogue masking leaks held-out geometry.</li><li><strong>SSL causal benefit:</strong> no random-encoder control, more input weights in the SSL head, no held-out reconstruction set, only six passes. Loss reduction does not imply geological specificity.</li><li><strong>Authenticated original sources:</strong> data were restored automatically from pinned owner mirrors, not a lawful organizer login. Template/value irregularities and ambiguous aliases remain open.</li><li><strong>Experiment-time Git ancestry:</strong> H27 receipts record the freeze IDs, but this PR clone lacks those commit objects. Source/input hashes match; ancestry cannot be reauthenticated until the original objects are restored.</li><li><strong>Native 1 m regional download:</strong> official metadata only; binary/full-region obtainability, vertical datum and seam processing still need verification on an unrestricted runner.</li><li><strong>A live leaderboard feed or unattended submission:</strong> not implemented because Terms prohibit automatic access. Eligibility/account-holder attestations cannot be supplied by an agent.</li><li><strong>Confirmed geothermal vents:</strong> no field, well, independent heat/fluid or reservoir validation.</li></ul><h2 id="next">Next session, in priority order</h2><ol><li>Reread the complete README prompt and preserve every negative holdout. Do not retune revealed H26/H27 folds or quadrants, create an H27 TIFF, or rename an archived OOF file as current.</li><li>Prioritize independent fault truth and genuinely untouched spatial validation; repeated known-catalogue draws are not independent unknown-fault evidence.</li><li>Resolve organizer-authenticated band semantics (<code>tc</code>, conductive-base depth, strain aliases), exact template provenance and full official data coverage.</li><li>Keep H27-COMCAT-RIDGE, H27-RAD-ALTER and H27-CHANNEL-DEFLECT deferred until source bytes/coverage and an independent test design are defensible. Only then rank and preregister a fresh slate.</li><li>For any later self-supervised research, require random-frozen-encoder/matched-parameter controls and spatially held-out unlabeled reconstruction evaluation.</li><li>No candidate is approved for a weekly slot. Any eventual eligibility, deadline confirmation and upload remain account-holder tasks; preserve each failed run.</li></ol><h2>Everyday use, without an install</h2><p class="small-note">The landing and guide expose the research TIFF immediately. The history table is searchable; source/feature/result inventories are downloadable CSVs. Scheduled Pages builds refresh permitted metadata and retain visible last-good records/errors. Python reproduction runs locally/on a suitable runner; the browser export only re-encodes frozen cells.</p></section>'''
